  "APIProfile": "Basic",
  "OnDegraded": "Continue",
  "Description": "The Personality Alignment (PGM-PAL) AIM decides the stance the A-User should adopt and produces the A-User State that the A-User Formation AIM renders. It is a reasoning AIM: knowing how the User feels and the context of the interaction, it judges what stance is appropriate for the A-User, which is not the same as mirroring the User. If the User laughs, the A-User laughing may be appropriate in a pub but improper in a church; the Personality Alignment AIM makes that judgement. To make it, the Personality Alignment AIM needs two things only: the User's internal state and the context. It receive",
